The underlying ...bug? inconsistency? phenomenon? ... is 
that monster AC works differently than player AC. No 
matter how low you get your AC with enchanted armor, 
monsters always have a chance to hit you, because they 
are ACTUALLY rolling against a number between -1 and 
your listed AC. You, on the other hand, have to roll 
against monster's full listed AC. So if a monster 
obtains some highly enchanted armor, they can end up 
being unhitable (because your attacks are 
affected only by the d20 role, the lowest % chance
to hit you can have is 5%. Even one more point
of AC beyond that point means you have a 0% chance
to hit).

Since such highly enchanted armor is not generated 
randomly by the game, the only way that monsters can 
get AC that low is from other players, as you found :).

...As an aside, in dNethack, monsters that equip more
than 10 points worth of armor use rules similar to 
those used for players, so this scenario would play
out differently in that variant.

